From 46ee68bcf030ef0b816365556b73012e07abda8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:30:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Show the frames rendered for windows of other
 processes.

A Wayland surface cannot be made part of another client, so a process
that renders into a window of another one, as the GPU process of a
Chromium based application does, shows nothing. Create a headless Vulkan
surface for such a window, send the frames to the process that owns the
window, and show them in a subsurface of the window.
